target:    tests/oracle/classify.py
gate:      composer test:classifier-plants
kind:      guard-removal
expect:    P32-a-registered-old-error-still-needs-the-oracle label
rationale: Drops the oracle term from old-errored-registered, which is how S4 shipped: a register hit plus an OLD error granted label (a)/pass with the oracle's verdict computed and discarded. (a) means NEW PROVEN CORRECT; a pre-blind register entry is evidence that a difference EXISTS and never evidence about its direction, so without this conjunct any arithmetic defect in v6's funnels rides in behind R4/R5 - the entries covering the exact surfaces v6 rewrote. The sibling rule emitting the same label (new-backed-registered) always carried the term; this one did not, and P19's oracle happened to agree with NEW, so the strong and the weak rule were indistinguishable to the whole plant set.
---
diff --git a/tests/oracle/classify.py b/tests/oracle/classify.py
--- a/tests/oracle/classify.py
+++ b/tests/oracle/classify.py
@@ -314,8 +314,7 @@ RULES = (
         "PROVEN CORRECT, and a registered OLD failure is evidence that the difference EXISTS, "
         "never evidence that the number NEW put in its place is right. Accepted for existence; "
         "if the entry is pre-blind its DIRECTION is not",
-        lambda f: (f.old_class == "error" and f.register_hit is not None
-                   and f.agrees(f.oracle_new)),
+        lambda f: (f.old_class == "error" and f.register_hit is not None),
     ),
     Rule(
         "old-errored", "SQL-error",
